   "## The control this report reconciliation needs",
   "Outsourced Service keeps report reconciliation visible because a service queue can look calm while the client promise, the SLA clock, and the responsible owner disagree. The service lead also checks the request, the SLA clock, the destination record, and the named owner before the case leaves the queue. For report reconciliation, the written sequence ends with a named reviewer and a date before the service lead releases the result. Outsourced Service records this step with the request ID, the SLA clock, the service reviewer, and the destination ticket system; case note 2 stays with the service record.",
   "Outsourced Service keeps report reconciliation visible because a service queue can look calm while the client promise, the SLA clock, and the responsible owner disagree. The service lead also checks the request, the SLA clock, the destination record, and the named owner before the case leaves the queue. For report reconciliation, the written sequence ends with a named reviewer and a date before the service lead releases the result. Outsourced Service records this step with the request ID, the SLA clock, the service reviewer, and the destination ticket system; case note 3 stays with the service record.",
   "## What the report reconciliation record must show",
