   "The report reconciliation record connects the request, the client, the source, the observation date, the reviewer, and the destination field. Missing and confirmed-negative evidence stay separate. The shift handoff keeps the open ticket, the client promise, the last response, and the next check together. For report reconciliation, the written sequence ends with a named reviewer and a date before the service lead releases the result. Outsourced Service records this step with the request ID, the SLA clock, the service reviewer, and the destination ticket system; case note 5 stays with the service record.",
